title: Blood on the Königsplatz
subtitle: The Security Police fire on a crowd outside the Reichstag.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1920 and month = 1
max-visits: 1
priority: 3
on-arrival: {!
RG.district('berlin', {repression: 8, militancy: 6});
RG.news('Security Police fire on the crowd outside the Reichstag: forty-two dead', 3);
!}

= Blood on the Königsplatz

On 13 January the National Assembly debated the Works Councils Law. The councils of 1918 had demanded control of the factories. The law lets them read the balance sheet and speak on dismissals, and forbids them to strike.

A hundred thousand Berlin workers filled the square in protest. The Security Police opened fire from the steps of the Reichstag with rifles and machine guns. Forty-two people are dead. The law passes the next week, and the first council elections are set for the spring.

[? if e19_council_lists = 1 : Since the summer our people have been drawing up lists in the big works. They are ready. ?]

- @strike: Call Berlin out against the murderers.
- @lists: Stand communist lists in every council election.
- @network: Link the councils into a network of their own, with Däumig and Richard Müller.
- @boycott: Boycott the councils of the law.

@strike
subtitle: Some factories will stop. The police have the lists of our shop stewards.
on-arrival: {!
Q.massacre_response = 1;
RG.startStrike('berlin', true);
RG.district('berlin', {repression: 8, loyalty: 4});
Q.lean_offensive += 1;
!}

Our call goes out from a cellar print shop. The AEG works and Siemensstadt stop for two days. A dozen of our stewards are arrested at the gates.

@lists
subtitle: [? if e19_council_lists = 1 : The lists are drawn up already. ?] Slow work, and it puts us where the workers vote.
on-arrival: {!
Q.massacre_response = 3;
Q.works_councils_line = 1;
Q.worker_support += Q.e19_council_lists ? 6 : 3;
if (Q.e19_council_lists) { RG.district('berlin', {members: 0.08}); RG.district('halle', {members: 0.08}); }
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
!}

[? if e19_council_lists = 1 : By April our lists hold seats in the machine shops of Berlin, the Leuna works and the yards of the coast. The union officials did not see them coming. ?][? if e19_council_lists = 0 : Our lists win a few hundred seats in the first month. In most works the union men are elected unopposed. ?]

@network
subtitle: [? if lock_councils = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The USPD left will come closer. The employers will call it sedition.
choose-if: lock_councils < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids it.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_councils == 1) { Q.unity -= 10; Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10; }
Q.massacre_response = 2;
Q.works_councils_line = 3;
Q.uspd_relation += 6;
Q.uspd_score += 1;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
!}

A Berlin centre of works councils meets in a hall in Neukölln. Its resolutions go well beyond the law, and the USPD left sits on its executive beside us.

@boycott
subtitle: The most bitter workers will agree. Most will vote in the elections anyway.
view-if: ultraleft_gone = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.massacre_response = 4;
Q.works_councils_line = 4;
Q.worker_support -= 3;
Q.ultraleft_satisfaction += 10;
Q.lean_ultraleft += 2;
!}

We tell the workers to have nothing to do with councils made by the men who shot them. In the shipyards of Hamburg and Bremen many tear up their union cards.
